# OpenAlgo research jobs for an always-on Linux server (Ubuntu 24.04).
# Linux equivalent of the Windows scheduled tasks in scripts/algo_backtest/windows/.
#
# 1. The server clock must be India time. Cron reads the server clock, not your location:
#        sudo timedatectl set-timezone Asia/Kolkata
#    Check with:  timedatectl        (the line "Time zone" must say Asia/Kolkata)
#
# 2. Open the crontab of the openalgo user with:  crontab -e
#    Paste the lines below, then check them with:  crontab -l
#    Replace /home/openalgo/openalgo-cloud with the real clone path if it differs.
#    The scripts must be executable:  chmod +x /home/openalgo/openalgo-cloud/scripts/algo_backtest/linux/*.sh
#
# 3. The jobs run Monday to Friday only. On an exchange holiday they still run, find no
#    market data and say so in their log; that is expected.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/home/openalgo/.local/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

# Bid and ask snapshots (entry and exit times the tests use).
15 10 * * 1-5 /home/openalgo/openalgo-cloud/scripts/algo_backtest/linux/snapshot_bidask.sh 1015
30 14 * * 1-5 /home/openalgo/openalgo-cloud/scripts/algo_backtest/linux/snapshot_bidask.sh 1430
0 15 * * 1-5 /home/openalgo/openalgo-cloud/scripts/algo_backtest/linux/snapshot_bidask.sh 1500

# Nightly option candle capture and the chain after it.
0 16 * * 1-5 /home/openalgo/openalgo-cloud/scripts/algo_backtest/linux/nightly.sh

# Daily checks: morning, midday and evening.
20 9 * * 1-5 /home/openalgo/openalgo-cloud/scripts/algo_backtest/linux/daily_check.sh morning
30 10 * * 1-5 /home/openalgo/openalgo-cloud/scripts/algo_backtest/linux/daily_check.sh midday
30 16 * * 1-5 /home/openalgo/openalgo-cloud/scripts/algo_backtest/linux/daily_check.sh evening

# Weekly update of both repositories, Sunday at 03:00. Off until you uncomment it.
# Only fast-forward pulls: a pull that would need a merge stops and leaves the work alone.
# 0 3 * * 0 cd /home/openalgo/openalgo-cloud && git pull --ff-only && cd /home/openalgo/openalgo-data && git pull --ff-only
